.TH SPROV 8 "@VERSION@" "sprov @VERSION@" "System Administration"
.SH NAME
sprov \- declarative storage provisioning executor
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B sprov
.RB [ \-n | \-\-dry\-run ]
.RB [ \-v ]...
.RB [ \-q ]...
.RB [ \-\-script ]
.RB [ \-\-no\-cleanup\-first ]
.I SPEC
.br
.B sprov \-\-version
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B sprov
reads a YAML specification describing a storage topology as a directed
acyclic graph (hardware, partitions, RAID, LUKS, LVM, filesystems) and
either executes the operations in topological order against live block
devices, or emits a busybox-compatible POSIX shell script that
performs the same operations when invoked.
.PP
Every filesystem
.B mountpoint
is rooted beneath the
.B control.path
prefix declared in the spec: with
.B control.path
= \fI/target\fR, a mountpoint of \fI/boot\fR becomes \fI/target/boot\fR.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-n ", " \-\-dry\-run
Log every command that would run without actually forking subprocesses.
.TP
.BR \-v ", " \-\-verbose
Increase verbosity. Repeatable: \fB\-v\fR, \fB\-vv\fR, \fB\-vvv\fR
progress from \fInormal\fR to \fIdebug\fR, which echoes every argv,
exit code, stdout, and stderr line.
.TP
.BR \-q ", " \-\-quiet
Decrease verbosity (down to \fIsilent\fR — warnings and errors only).
.TP
.B \-\-script
Emit a POSIX shell script to stdout equivalent to the live-execution
path, then exit. The script targets dash/busybox, uses
.BR set (1)
.B \-eu
for strictness, and handles stdin payloads (passphrases) via quoted
heredocs so secrets never appear in
.BR ps (1)
output.
.TP
.B \-\-no\-cleanup\-first
Skip the pre-flight
.BR umount (8)
of
.B control.path
that normally precedes execution. Useful when iterating on a spec
against a freshly-booted installer with a guaranteed-clean state.
.TP
.B \-\-version
Print the version and exit.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Success.
.TP
.B 1
Spec validation failed — bad YAML, unknown node type, missing
required field, cycle in the DAG, unresolved parent id.
.TP
.B 2
Execution failed while running a node; reverse cleanup of
already-succeeded nodes is attempted before exit.
.TP
.B 64
CLI usage error — missing spec argument, unreadable spec file.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I SPEC
YAML file with two top-level keys:
.B vars
(optional mapping of template variables) and
.B storage
(list of node entries). See
.B EXAMPLES
for the expected shape.
.SH SUPPORTED NODE TYPES
.B control, hardware, partition, raid1, dm\-crypt\-luks, lvm\-pv,
.B lvm\-vg, lvm\-lv, filesystem.
.SH EXAMPLES
.PP
Generate a shell script for offline inspection:
.PP
.RS
.nf
sprov \-\-script /etc/sprov/install.yaml > /tmp/install.sh
sh \-n /tmp/install.sh   # syntax-only validation
.fi
.RE
.PP
Dry-run with full debug logging:
.PP
.RS
.nf
sprov \-\-dry\-run \-vvv /etc/sprov/install.yaml
.fi
.RE
.SH AUTHOR
c0dev0id <sh+git@codevoid.de>
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR parted (8),
.BR mdadm (8),
.BR cryptsetup (8),
.BR lvm (8),
.BR mkfs (8),
.BR mount (8)
